Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['Causal sequence masking
does not prevent target contamination through the graph: each training 
transition also contributes to the fixed graph used to predict that transition. 
This is not held-out-label leakage, but can inflate training margins and 
encourage reliance on edges unavailable for unseen continuations. Compare 
leave-one-transition-out counts or cross-fitted graphs.', 'A residual weight 
initialized at zero and implemented with clamp(weight, 0, 2) can become stuck 
below zero, where its gradient vanishes. Specify a trainable bounded 
parameterization, initialization, and optimizer behavior that preserve the 
intended baseline starting point.', "The additive residual only boosts supported
candidates; it does not directly suppress stale interests or establish immediate
usefulness. With positional weights exp(-lag), the fifth item's weight is 
approximately 0.018, so claims about repeated evidence across five items require
qualification. Missing support thresholds also allow a single observed 
transition to receive maximum outgoing probability.", 'Reproducibility requires 
explicit graph tie-breaking, treatment of padding and repeated items, 
score-scale calibration, candidate tensor shapes, and safe handling of sequence 
context through the diagnostic interface. A mutable cache in log2feats risks 
associating scores with the wrong sequence.', 'The evaluation plan lacks 
popularity and graph-support controls, checkpoint-selection rules, and a trial 
allocation within the 43,200 GPU-second budget. With only 200 validation users 
per category, small gains and repeated hyperparameter selection need cautious 
interpretation. Originality 5 and difficulty 3 appear optimistic without a 
closer comparison to first-order Markov score fusion and a concrete sparse 
implementation.'], generating follow-up queries
