configurations and record this difference from baseline; a future encoder-only clipping control would be needed to isolate its effect. Existing baseline regularization applies unchanged to baseline parameters; new branch parameters receive no explicit regularizer.\n\nAt each position t, pool sequence[t] and up to K-1 preceding valid items, using weights proportional to decay^lag, normalized by the valid weight sum. Mask after projection and normalization because padding embeddings alone do not mask downstream operations. Return zero for empty histories. Exclude padded positive targets from loss. All pooling is causal; target items and future events never enter prefix features. Repeated occurrences receive multiple terms, but this is not a learned measure of recurring semantic interest. The scorer can learn popularity, repeat-purchase, or common-transition shortcuts, and older useful persistent interests can be suppressed. Report actual validation differences rather than claiming that these mechanisms resolve satisfaction or prerequisites.\n\nFor baseline, bypass branch construction, computation, regularization, and optimizer registration entirely. Preserve baseline initialization order and random-number streams; unchanged seeds alone do not ensure equivalence. For residual runs, construct and initialize the branch inside torch.random.fork_rng, including the relevant CUDA device if CUDA random draws occur, after baseline initialization. The branch contains no stochastic forward operations. This preserves baseline random draws at initialization but does not imply identical optimization trajectories.\n\nExpose concatenated encoder and scaled, gated source features through log2feats. predict_score must construct matching candidate target features and support aligned B x L training items and B x C candidate lists without accidental cross-user broadcasting. Retain view.model as the actual trained nn.Module and view.item_emb as the base embedding table. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device) and run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. Compute margins with the complete combined scorer. Label embedding cosine diagnostics as base-table measurements, not measurements of the entire transition operator. Omit unavailable category breakdowns or mark them unavailable without inventing metadata. Update the predictor writer to serialize architecture version, projection dimensions, normalization settings, gate mode, K, decay, alpha, checkpoint state, and routing; reconstruct exactly the training scorer. Verify on a small public-history batch that saved/reloaded candidate scores agree, padding is inert, and changing a future sequence suffix does not affect earlier features. These checks require no hidden test data.\n\nAllocate at most 9,000 GPU-seconds to each configuration across all four categories, including its training and routine validation; reserve 7,200 seconds of the 43,200-second total for diagnostics, debugging, and failures. Before full comparisons, use baseline timing counted against its allocation to set a common epoch cap that fits the allocations, with a maximum of the environment epoch setting; freeze that cap for all configurations. If a run cannot complete the common cap, retain the largest previously completed common checkpoint epoch for every configuration rather than favoring a partially trained category. Evaluate only the final common checkpoint per configuration for selection. Log all comparisons and costs. Select the largest unrounded equal-weight macro validation HR@10, with baseline preferred on ties and the listed configuration order resolving remaining ties. Preserve the host's 200 users/category, 99 unique negatives, and evaluation seed 42; do not modify its evaluator or introduce alternate selection metrics.\n\nIf the existing host output exposes per-user hits on identical candidates, compute paired differences within category and bootstrap users within each category 10,000 times using a separate NumPy generator seeded 42; report the percentile 95% interval, category differences, and baseline-only versus variant-only hit counts. Do not reimplement or modify the host evaluator to obtain these outputs; if unavailable, state that uncertainty analysis is unavailable. One changed hit moves category HR by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR by 0.125 points. Intervals condition on fixed trained models and candidates, omit seed and candidate variability, and do not correct selection optimism. Restrict simulator feedback to descriptive diagnostics from twenty users, without further tuning. Sampled HR gains do not establish full-catalog retrieval, diversity, satisfaction, or compatibility improvements.",
  "pseudocode": "CONFIGS = [\n    baseline,\n    residual(K=5, decay=0.7, gate='context', alpha=0.1, d=32),\n    residual(K=5, decay=0.7, gate='one', alpha=0.1, d=32),\n    residual(K=1, decay=0.7, gate='context', alpha=0.1, d=32),\n]\n\nclass RecentDirectionalSASRec(nn.Module):\n    def log2feats(self, sequence):\n        h = self.sasrec.log2feats(sequence)       # B,L,H\n        valid = sequence.ne(0)\n        a = self.source_norm(self.source_projection(self.item_emb(sequence)))\n        a = a * valid.unsqueeze(-1)              # mask after all transforms\n        r = zeros_like(a)\n        denom = zeros_like(valid, dtype=a.dtype)\n        for lag in range(self.K):\n            shifted_a = causal_shift_right(a, lag, fill=0)\n            shifted_valid = causal_shift_right(valid, lag, fill=False)\n            weight = (self.decay ** lag) * shifted_valid\n            r += weight.unsqueeze(-1) * shifted_a\n            denom += weight\n        r = r / denom.clamp_min(1e-12).unsqueeze(-1)\n        r = r * valid.unsqueeze(-1)\n        g = sigmoid(self.gate(h)) if self.gate_mode == 'context' else 1.0\n        return concatenate([h, self.alpha * g * r / sqrt(self.d)], dim=-1)\n\n    def candidate_features(self, items):\n        e = self.item_emb(items)\n        b = self.target_norm(self.target_projection(e))\n        b = b * items.ne(0).unsqueeze(-1)\n        return concatenate([e, b], dim=-1)\n\n    def predict_score(self, features, items):\n        # Explicitly choose aligned dot for B,L targets or batched\n        # matrix multiplication for B,C candidate lists.\n        return shape_checked_dot(features, self.candidate_features(items))\n\nfor config in CONFIGS:\n    for category in ORIGINAL_FOUR_CATEGORIES:\n        set_training_seed(42)\n        model = construct_unchanged_baseline()\n        if config != baseline:\n            with fork_rng_preserving_baseline_state():\n                model = attach_initialized_residual(model, config)\n        optimizer = baseline_optimizer_with_unregularized_branch_group(model)\n        for epoch in range(COMMON_EPOCH_CAP):\n            for _, sequence, positive, negative in train_loader:\n                f = model.log2feats(sequence)\n                pos = model.predict_score(f, positive)\n                neg = model.predict_score(f, negative)\n                loss = unchanged_baseline_loss(pos, neg, valid=positive.ne(0))\n                optimizer.zero_grad()\n                loss.backward()\n                if config != baseline:\n                    clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), 5.0)\n                optimizer.step()\n        save_complete_model_configuration_and_state(trial_directory)\n    write_predictor_with_identical_architecture_scoring_and_category_routing()\n    # Existing host evaluates the final common checkpoint.\n    log_host_macro_and_category_validation_HR10_and_GPU_cost()\n# Select once by pinned macro validation HR@10; baseline wins ties.\n# Run compatible diagnostics; do not use them for additional adaptive tuning.",
