Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe uses item embeddings and sequence-conditioned scores. Model 
architecture is not supplied, so representation internals cannot be verified. 
`log2feats(sequence)` produces per-position features; `predict_score(features, 
items)` scores positive and negative items at each position. Diagnosis examines 
all valid training positions, rather than explicitly selecting the final 
sequence representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view 
and references its `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Reviews and 
histories are not directly analyzed.

The loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped B ×
L. Sequences are converted to NumPy before calling `log2feats`. Positive and 
negative IDs are stacked into B × L × 2 candidate tensors. Positions with 
positive ID zero are excluded. Margin evaluation calls `eval()` and disables 
gradients; the previous training mode is not restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Excludes padding embedding zero, samples up to
2,048 item embeddings with seed 42, normalizes them, and averages off-diagonal 
cosine similarities. Mapping through `(mean_cos + 1) / 2` gives a collapse 
indicator: higher suggests stronger directional alignment; approximately 0.5 
indicates average cosine near zero.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower-tail 
positive-minus-negative logit margins across up to ten loader batches. Higher 
values indicate stronger separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction below 0.5; lower indicates fewer 
weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts low-margin and incorrectly 
ranked positions, plus the twenty most frequent metadata categories for positive
and negative items separately. These are raw counts, not exposure-normalized 
error rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, or sensitivity test runs. Randomness 
only subsamples embeddings; negatives come from the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate 
prompt requests an interpreted JSON summary containing `status`, 
`core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`.

Available metadata lacks item categories, so category lists remain empty. Probes
measure training-pair separation and embedding alignment, not validation HR@10, 
full-catalog quality, temporal sensitivity, or user traits. Margins depend on 
logit scale and negative sampling. Empty valid samples produce zero-valued 
margin metrics, which require cautious interpretation.

