om the latest valid observed position. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model must be the actual trained module; log2feats must return fused features and predict_score must match inference. Retain view.item_emb, user_train, meta_data, and review_data compatibility without fabricating unavailable fields. Mark category breakdowns unavailable when category metadata is absent. Track baseline and residual norms, alpha, margin p10, and negative-over-positive rates; margins are scale-sensitive secondary diagnostics, not selection criteria. Predeclare four configurations: unchanged SASRec, zero-fixed recent-five control, learned last-item residual, and learned recent-five residual. Each retains all four categories and seed 42. Use the baseline checkpoint evaluation schedule and stopping policy unchanged, record that resolved schedule before execution, and do not add extra inspected checkpoints. Enforce the shared 43,200 GPU-second limit including diagnostics and failures; log every attempt and stop before launching work that cannot fit the remaining allocation. Select by pinned four-category macro validation HR@10; break exact ties by unchanged baseline first, then fewer added operations, then earlier checkpoint. More elaborate controls—masked mean pooling, a tuned constant residual, history-conditioned scalar/vector gates, and attention pooling—remain deferred hypotheses. A conditioned gate could use causal prefix length, adjacent embedding cosine agreement, and pooled-feature agreement, but these signals are proxies and can learn popularity or recency shortcuts. Save per-user validation hits if exposed by the existing evaluator; do not modify the evaluator to obtain them. With available hit indicators, use 10,000 paired bootstrap replicates with analysis seed 42, independently resampling 200 users within each category and applying identical indices to both models. Average the four category differences equally and report the observed difference and 95% percentile interval. One changed hit changes category HR@10 by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR@10 by 0.125 points. Intervals condition on trained models and fixed candidates, exclude seed/candidate variability, and do not remove winner-selection bias. Treat tiny improvements or intervals spanning zero as inconclusive. Freeze selection before the host's held-out evaluation. Full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for the twenty diagnostic users remain qualitative evidence rather than the selection metric.",
