Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis uses item embeddings and sequence-conditioned scores. 
`item_emb.weight` supplies item vectors; `log2feats(sequence)` computes 
per-position sequence representations; `predict_score(features, items)` scores 
positive and negative items at each position. The model implementation is 
absent, so the encoder architecture and exact representation computation cannot 
be verified. This probe evaluates all valid positions, rather than selecting a 
final user vector.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` receives the compatibility view and stores its 
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently 
consulted; stored reviews and histories are unused.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` processes up to ten batches of `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`, with tensors shaped B × L. Sequences pass 
through `log2feats`; stacked positive/negative IDs pass to `predict_score`. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Scoring runs in evaluation mode 
without gradients; the previous training mode is not restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, and averages off-diagonal cosine similarities. 
Mapping via `(mean_cosine + 1)/2` produces the score. Higher values indicate 
directional alignment; roughly 0.5 corresponds to near-zero average similarity, 
not necessarily collapse.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and tenth percentile of
positive-minus-negative logits. Higher values indicate stronger separation, 
including among difficult positions.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction below 0.5; lower indicates fewer 
weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts positive/negative item 
categories separately for low-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, retaining
the top twenty categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, shuffling, ablations, or sensitivity tests.
Random sampling only limits embedding analysis; negatives come from the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate prompt 
requests an interpreted JSON summary containing status, findings, implications, 
and evidence; it does not itself execute interpretation.

These training-batch probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, generalization, or simulator traits. Margins depend on score scale and 
negative sampling. Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category 
lists should be empty; counts cannot establish category-specific weaknesses. 
Mean cosine alone cannot establish representation diversity or rank.

