{
  "description": "Add a zero-initialized scalar recency-pooling residual to each dataset's SASRec model, accompanied by final-prefix rank diagnostics and controlled attribution comparisons.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests recent, repeated interests sometimes receive insufficient influence. A direct recency path is a feasible initial hypothesis, but feedback does not establish that recency causes benchmark errors. Exact zero initialization preserves the baseline's initial predictions. Paired perturbations and simple pooling controls help distinguish recent-content dependence from ordering effects, additional parameters, or popularity shortcuts. Only the unchanged official macro validation HR@10 determines selection.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four category routes, original splits, single-GPU execution, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Write all checkpoints, logs, and generated predictor files beneath the trial directory. Preserve the baseline architecture, embedding initialization, loss, optimizer, sampler, batch size, and learning-rate schedule for the first comparison. Do not assume the baseline matches a modern pre-LN Transformer: integrate at its actual final sequence-feature output. Use raw shared item embeddings for the new pool, without positional embeddings, input dropout, or square-root embedding scaling; apply a separate LayerNorm with the baseline's epsilon before residual addition. Use fixed tau=5 and unconstrained scalar alpha=0, with no final renormalization. These are proposed settings, not validated optima. The pool is causal at every supervised position. Alpha=0 initially blocks task gradients to branch-exclusive LayerNorm parameters, while shared embeddings still receive baseline gradients. Log alpha, pre/post-normalization pool norms, baseline feature norms, and residual-to-baseline norm ratios. Save alpha and residual normalization parameters in every checkpoint and update the predictor writer with the identical architecture and configuration. Keep view.model bound to the actual trained nn.Module; view.log2feats must return residual-adjusted features and view.predict_score must preserve the existing candidate-scoring contract.\n\nBefore observing new results, freeze the baseline's checkpoint schedule, evaluated epochs, and any existing stopping rule, then use the same policy for every variant. If the baseline has no documented checkpoint schedule, use every 20 epochs and the final epoch. Select one common epoch across the four category models by their equal-weight macro validation HR@10; break ties by earlier epoch, then prefer the baseline architecture. Use a bounded attribution ladder: baseline, learned-gate last-item residual, learned-gate uniform-pooling residual, and learned-gate exponential-pooling residual. If budget remains after this preregistered set, separately test exponential pooling alone and a fixed-alpha=0.1 exponential residual; log these as additional comparisons. Raw-versus-scaled pooling and normalization-after-addition are possible later ablations, not requirements for the initial bounded search. Do not infer a learned-gate benefit without a fixed-weight comparison. Record every trial and checkpoint comparison, including failures. Account for all training and diagnostic GPU time within 43,200 GPU-seconds; start no additional trial whose estimated cost exceeds the remaining budget. Keep the baseline as an eligible result if the ladder cannot be completed.\n\nDiagnosisProbe.run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) must return metrics and metric_definitions and restore model mode using try/finally. Preserve embedding-alignment and positive/negative-margin measurements, valid-position counts, and their scale/sampling limitations. Mark unavailable category metadata explicitly rather than producing category evidence. Freeze up to 50 eligible users per category, sorted by user ID and sampled with seed 42 if necessary; derive one replay example per user by withholding their final training interaction and retaining the preceding baseline-length prefix. Skip users without a prefix and report counts. This replay target was used during model fitting and is not a generalization measurement. Freeze replay candidate IDs, order, and tie rules across models and perturbations. For an auxiliary replay audit, choose up to 99 unique non-target items with seed 42, record its sampling policy, and never describe this as the official validation evaluator. Optional uniform, target-popularity-matched, and title/description TF-IDF negative pools require separately recorded deterministic sampling rules and remain hypotheses to validate. A chunked full-catalog replay audit is diagnostic only; exclude prefix-consumed items except the target itself, which must remain eligible even if repeated. These auxiliary policies must never replace host candidates or filtering.\n\nFor each prefix, preserve the final interaction and delete k=min(3, floor((n-1)/2)) preceding interactions. Compare deletion of the k most recent eligible interactions with uniformly sampled deletion of k eligible interactions. Use perturbation seeds 42, 43, and 44 for random deletions and last-item-preserving shuffles; skip deletion when k=0. Run both compact-and-left-pad deletion and in-place masking, keeping the final prediction position fixed. In-place masking must update the actual attention key-padding mask, including internal holes, prevent invalid all-masked attention rows from producing NaNs, and zero padded outputs. Record rank changes, diagnostic HR@10 changes, top-10 overlap, and feature cosine changes as paired per-user quantities. Deletion and masking remain different interventions with different confounds; neither identifies intent or a causal effect.\n\nUse untouched validation transitions and official per-user hits for generalization comparisons only if the existing host interface exposes them. Never reconstruct hidden evaluator state, regenerate host negatives, filter out a legitimate repeated target, or modify candidate order and tie-breaking. Report repeat-target/novel-target and history-length strata when exposed; mark unavailable measurements null with a reason and count. Training-prefix replay, full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for the twenty training users, and official sampled validation answer different questions. Retain the required five users per category for qualitative assessment; do not infer diversity or conformity traits. Titles and descriptions can support explicit evidence, but cannot establish equipment ownership, practical compatibility, unwanted duplication, ratings, or intent. Do not use unavailable