  "pseudocode": "class RecencyResidualSASRec(SASRec):\n    initialize alpha = Parameter(0.0)\n    initialize residual_norm = LayerNorm(hidden_dim, eps=baseline_eps)\n\n    log2feats(sequence):\n        h = baseline_log2feats(sequence)\n        e = item_emb(sequence)  # raw shared embeddings\n        numerator = zeros(batch_size, hidden_dim)\n        denominator = zeros(batch_size, 1)\n        outputs = []\n        decay = exp(-1 / 5.0)\n        for t in sequence_positions:\n            valid = (sequence[:, t] != 0)[:, None]\n            numerator = decay * numerator + valid * e[:, t]\n            denominator = decay * denominator + valid\n            recent = numerator / clamp_min(denominator, 1e-8)\n            combined = h[:, t] + alpha * residual_norm(recent)\n            outputs.append(combined * valid)\n        return stack(outputs, dim=1)\n\n# Controls use the same branch normalization and scalar initialization:\n# last-item: recent = e[:, t]\n# uniform: use decay = 1\n# exponential: use decay = exp(-1/5)\n# pooling-only, if budgeted: return residual_norm(recent) at valid positions\n# fixed-weight, if budgeted: replace learned alpha with constant 0.1\n\nclass DiagnosisProbe:\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        prior_mode = view.model.training\n        try:\n            view.model.eval()\n            with no_grad():\n                metrics = existing_embedding_and_margin_probes(train_loader)\n                replay = frozen_training_prefix_examples(seed=42, max_users_per_category=50)\n                candidates = load_or_create_frozen_replay_candidates(replay, seed=42)\n                original = measure_ranks_hits_top10_features(replay, candidates)\n                for perturbation_seed in [42, 43, 44]:\n                    for example in replay:\n                        n = count_nonpadding(example.prefix)\n                        k = min(3, (n - 1) // 2)\n                        if k == 0:\n                            record_skip(example)\n                            continue\n                        eligible = positions_before_last_nonpadding(example.prefix)\n                        recent_positions = eligible[-k:]\n                        random_positions = sample_without_replacement(\n                            eligible, k, seed=(perturbation_seed, example.user_id))\n                        for mode in ['compact_left_pad', 'mask_in_place']:\n                            recent = remove_positions(example, recent_positions, mode)\n                            control = remove_positions(example, random_positions, mode)\n                            preserve_final_prediction_position(recent, control)\n                            measure_paired_changes(original, recent, control, candidates)\n                        shuffled = shuffle_nonpadding_preserving_last(\n                            example, seed=(perturbation_seed, example.user_id))\n                        measure_paired_changes(original, shuffled, candidates)\n                metrics.update(aggregate_by_user_category_length_and_repeat_status())\n                record_missing_measurements_as_null_with_reason_and_count(metrics)\n                return {'metrics': metrics, 'metric_definitions': definitions}\n        finally:\n            view.model.train(prior_mode)\n\nfreeze trial ladder, checkpoint schedule, tie rules, candidate contracts, and budget ledger\nfor variant in preregistered_variants:\n    if estimated_trial_cost > remaining_search_budget:\n        break\n    train all four routed models using the prescribed seeds and matched settings\n    write architecture-matched predictor and checkpoints beneath the trial directory\n    obtain unchanged official macro validation HR@10 at preregistered checkpoints\n    log all comparisons and costs\n    if official per-user hits are exposed:\n        compute paired category-stratified bootstrap with 2000 replicates, seed=42\nselect by official macro validation HR@10; ties prefer earlier epoch, then baseline\nretain full artifact/configuration parity for final host inference",
