INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for diagnosis in iteration 1:
{
  "description": "Add an input-conditioned scalar gate that interpolates each per-dataset SASRec contextual feature with a LayerNorm-normalized mean of up to five causal input item embeddings. This is an incremental combination of established recent-item pooling and gated fusion, distinguished from HGN’s feature/instance gates and additive scoring, and SHAN’s two-stage attention. Use the identical representation during training, diagnosis and prediction.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests incidental or older interactions can crowd out recent, specific evidence. The branch offers a low-cost, falsifiable test of whether unordered recent-item information improves next-item ranking. The original proposal does not explicitly distinguish repeated interests from incidental events; repetition-specific benefits require additional stratified evidence. Histories do not reveal intent, continued ownership, satisfaction, prerequisite availability or compatibility. SASRec features already depend on history, so describing the interpolation as separate long-term and short-term preference modeling would overstate the distinction.",
  "implementation_notes": "Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], existing input splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four dataset routes and trial-local artifacts. Honor the SASREC_EPOCHS environment setting, whose host default is 200. Keep execution single-GPU. Preserve baseline optimizer, learning rate, loss, sampling, embedding initialization, batch size and checkpoint procedure initially; record their inherited values and every changed setting in the trial configuration.\n\nAt position t, take raw shared item embeddings before positional encoding and embedding dropout. Pool positions max(0,t-4)..t, excluding zero IDs and dividing by the number of valid IDs. The current input item is allowed; its next-item target must never enter this window. Apply a trainable LayerNorm(D) to the mean, initialized with scale one and bias zero. Use Linear(2D,1) on concatenated contextual and pooled features, with zero weights and bias -4, so the initial mean-branch gate is exactly sigmoid(-4), approximately 0.018. Interpolate the complete feature vectors and explicitly zero padding positions after normalization and interpolation. Compute pooling with causal cumulative sums and valid-count differences. With ordinary initialization, the model is close to, but not exactly, unchanged SASRec; include a branch-off endpoint to establish exact baseline behavior. LayerNorm does not equalize the norms of the two branches, so inspect feature norms and score scales alongside gates.\n\nTrain through the existing loss using positive != 0 as its validity mask. The shared item embedding receives gradients from both paths. Update the predictor writer so generated working/predict.py reconstructs the backbone, gate and normalization, loads all state parameters, uses the existing last-valid-position convention, and preserves dataset routing. Store window width and architectural configuration with each checkpoint. Verify causal pooling on padded sequences, absence of target leakage and numerical agreement between training-time evaluation and generated prediction.\n\nPreserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model must be the actual trained module; view.log2feats returns blended B x L x D features; view.item_emb exposes the shared embedding; view.predict_score supports B x L x 2 candidate IDs. Retain user_train, meta_data and review_data compatibility fields without fabricating unavailable contents. Set evaluation mode on view.model, disable gradients and restore its original mode afterward. Retain embedding alignment and margin diagnostics, but identify alignment as directional similarity rather than proof of collapse. Add valid-sample counts; empty measurements must be null rather than healthy-looking zero failure rates. Unavailable category breakdowns remain empty and explicitly unavailable.\n\nWithin the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget, prioritize unchanged SASRec, a fixed mixture with g=sigmoid(-4), and the conditioned gate, under identical inherited training settings. Use the same existing checkpoint-selection schedule and log actual GPU time. If budget permits, preregister a small extension: last-item-only, older-window and full-history pooling; mean-only and branch-off endpoints; a matched-parameter context-only adapter; and initialization logit 0 versus -4. Further window sizes 1/5/10/full, mean/max/attention pools, global versus conditioned/vector gates, and normalization ablations are optional follow-ups, not a required Cartesian search. Keep tuning effort comparable and report incomplete controls rather than implying they ran.\n\nFor inference sensitivity, freeze the checkpoint. Persist each user/cutoff's target, candidates, candidate order, original-history exclusions and tie-breaking once. Compare equal-sized recent/older edits, suffix-only histories and order shuffling using those same objects. Preserve the final item when testing within-window order, then test membership changes separately. Because mean pooling is permutation-invariant within a fixed window, surviving such shuffles does not demonstrate order modeling. Distinguish inference perturbations from separately retrained shuffling controls. Match replacement items on permitted training popularity and availability where possible, and compare with random edits and popularity-only scores.\n\nA checkpoint trained on a purported auxiliary target cannot support held-out generalization claims. To measure that, split permitted training histories before fitting a separate diagnostic backbone, then construct all training windows and learned statistics from the truncated data. Excluded targets must not reappear inside later windows. Freeze this separate model across perturbations. Per-user truncation supports a user-prefix experiment but not strict global temporal claims; those require global or rolling cutoffs across users. Restrict auxiliary candidates and metadata to prediction-time availability where known, labeling first interaction as only an availability proxy. If retraining is unaffordable, report training-history sensitivity instead. Never modify the host splits or evaluator.\n\nReport paired per-user validation differences by category, then their equal-weight macro average; use user-clustered uncertainty estimates when multiple prefixes share a user. These intervals do not measure training-seed variability. Inspect history length, training-frequency popularity strata, gate saturation and branch norms to detect popularity shortcuts or concentration of gains. Repeated validation selection can overfit the 800 pinned users: predeclare the small primary comparison, log all trials and avoid broad post hoc tuning. Select only with the pinned macro validation HR@10: 200 users/category, 99 unique negatives and evaluation seed 42. Auxiliary diagnostics, including full-catalog metrics from legitimate training-only holdouts, never replace that criterion. For the twenty real training users, report unseen-item overlap, popularity and coverage without claiming full-catalog accuracy, immediate purchase intent or observed diversity/conformity traits.",
  "pseudocode": "configuration = inherit_baseline_settings_and_record_changes()\nfor category in four_existing_routes:\n    model = SASRecWithRecentGate(width=5, gate_weight=0, gate_bias=-4)\n    for batch in existing_training_loader:\n        seq, pos, neg = batch.sequence, batch.positive, batch.negative\n        valid = (seq != 0)\n        h = model.backbone.log2feats(seq)\n        e = model.item_emb(seq) * valid[..., None]  # before positions/dropout\n        sums, counts = causal_window_sums_and_counts(e, valid, width=5)\n        mean = sums / counts.clamp_min(1)[..., None]\n        m = model.recent_norm(mean) * valid[..., None]\n        g = sigmoid(model.gate(concat(h, m)))\n        z = ((1 - g) * h + g * m) * valid[..., None]\n        loss = existing_loss(score(z, pos), score(z, neg), mask=(pos != 0))\n        optimize(loss)\n    save_all_parameters_and_configuration_beneath_trial_directory()\n    emit_predictor_with_identical_features_scoring_and_dataset_routing()\n    verify_predictor_parity_and_causal_padding_behavior()\nselect_using_existing_pinned_macro_validation_HR10()\n\n# Optional sensitivity analysis: this is not held-out generalization.\nfreeze(trained_checkpoint)\nrecords = persist_training_prefix_targets_candidates_original_exclusions_and_ties()\nfor intervention in predeclared_equal_size_history_edits:\n    score_identical_records_with_frozen_checkpoint(records, intervention)\nreport_paired_differences_as_training_history_sensitivity()\n\n# Optional generalization analysis, only if budget permits.\npermitted_prefixes, auxiliary_targets = split_training_histories_before_any_fit()\nwindows = construct_windows_only_from(permitted_prefixes)\ndiagnostic_model = train_from_scratch(windows, permitted_statistics_only=True)\nfreeze(diagnostic_model)\nrun_paired_interventions_with_fixed_targets_candidates_exclusions_and_ties()",
