      - Definitions: {"Movies_and_TV:history_edits": "Frozen-model sensitivity, not recommendation accuracy. Draws are averaged within user, then users equally. Five supplied users/category are exploratory, not representative. Aggregate four complete category reports externally with equal weights; never treat absent reports as zero.", "Movies_and_TV:matched_history_edit_contrasts": "Within-user differences between edit summaries, averaged equally across paired users. Require all preregistered draws in both conditions. Bootstrap paired user differences with 2000 seeded replicates. Negative overlap contrasts mean less overlap under the first edit; signs of other fields follow their definitions. These are sensitivity comparisons, not recommendation improvements. Users absent from every successful condition remain visible in panel metadata and failures.", "Movies_and_TV:top10_overlap": "Intersection of original and edited top min(10,C), divided by min(10,C); higher is greater stability, not necessarily greater accuracy.", "Movies_and_TV:top10_mean_absolute_rank_displacement": "Mean absolute change in zero-based full-catalog rank over the original top min(10,C); stable descending score sorting breaks ties by ascending item ID.", "Movies_and_TV:strict_pair_flip_rate": "Fraction of a fixed deterministic sample of at most 4096 distinct unordered candidate pairs whose strict ordering reverses. Exclude pairs tied in either condition; report ties and denominator. Undefined denominators return null.", "Movies_and_TV:raw_mean_absolute_score_change": "Mean absolute paired logit change. Scale-dependent; cannot be compared as accuracy or interpreted as invariant sensitivity.", "Movies_and_TV:feature_l2_change": "L2 change in the encoder's final feature at position L-1, separately from score/rank effects; representation-scale-dependent.", "Movies_and_TV:training_margins": "Mean, lower empirical p10, P(negative>positive), and P(margin<0.5) under the stated independent training-only diagnostic distribution. Not directly comparable to live-loader margins; raw values depend on logit scale. Missing cases are null, not zero.", "Movies_and_TV:embedding_geometry": "At most 2048 nonpadding rows sampled with a local seed-42 generator. Mean cosine measures directional alignment only. Centered singular-value entropy gives effective rank, normalized by min(n-1,d); leading mass uses singular values, not squared energy. Neither proves collapse or user diversity.", "Movies_and_TV:edit_policy": "Recent deletion removes the final item; old deletion retains it. Preanchor/early comparisons both retain the final item and use min(k,n-2) deletions. Random deletion has the same primary k and reports its final-item policy. Compaction changes positions as well as content; these are not retrained ablations.", "Movies_and_TV:exploratory_user_bootstrap_95_interval": "2000 seeded within-category user bootstrap replicates after averaging draws within user. Undefined with fewer than two users. Full-catalog stability differs from pinned sampled-candidate HR@10; adaptive-selection intervals remain exploratory.", "Movies_and_TV:selection_policy": "The unchanged host-pinned four-category macro validation HR@10 is the sole selection metric. One changed hit among 200 users/category changes macro HR@10 by 0.00125. No test outcomes, ratings, reviews, item categories, prices, stores, or simulator traits are used.", "Movies_and_TV:integrity": "Identity, repeated inference, and positive score-rescaling checks are observations, not assumed passes. All module flags and Python/NumPy/torch RNG state are restored; live training iterator and worker state are untouched.", "Movies_and_TV:diagnostic_cost": "Synchronized wall seconds for this call, including CPU preparation. On CUDA the same duration is reported as allocated single-GPU seconds for conservative search-budget accounting; this is not measured kernel-active time.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:history_edits": "Frozen-model sensitivity, not recommendation accuracy. Draws are averaged within user, then users equally. Five supplied users/category are exploratory, not representative. Aggregate four complete category reports externally with equal weights; never treat absent reports as zero.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:matched_history_edit_contrasts": "Within-user differences between edit summaries, averaged equally across paired users. Require all preregistered draws in both conditions. Bootstrap paired user differences with 2000 seeded replicates. Negative overlap contrasts mean less overlap under the first edit; signs of other fields follow their definitions. These are sensitivity comparisons, not recommendation improvements. Users absent from every successful condition remain visible in panel metadata and failures.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:top10_overlap": "Intersection of original and edited top min(10,C), divided by min(10,C); higher is greater stability, not necessarily greater accuracy.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:top10_mean_absolute_rank_displacement": "Mean absolute change in zero-based full-catalog rank over the original top min(10,C); stable descending score sorting breaks ties by ascending item ID.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:strict_pair_flip_rate": "Fraction of a fixed deterministic sample of at most 4096 distinct unordered candidate pairs whose strict ordering reverses. Exclude pairs tied in either condition; report ties and denominator. Undefined denominators return null.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:raw_mean_absolute_score_change": "Mean absolute paired logit change. Scale-dependent; cannot be compared as accuracy or interpreted as invariant sensitivity.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:feature_l2_change": "L2 change in the encoder's final feature at position L-1, separately from score/rank effects; representation-scale-dependent.", "Industrial_and_Scientific:training_margins": "Mean, lower empirical p10, P(negative>positive), and P(margin<0.5) under the stated independent training-