  "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies older or incidental interactions receiving excessive influence and broad relatedness crowding out specific current matches. Recent pooling provides an explicit local signal, while recent-conditioned historical pooling may recover supporting interests. These mechanisms explicitly address two user-facing failures, although their effects require validation. Electronics’ negative lower-tail margin motivates testing contextual discrimination. Normalized attention can represent relative multiplicity but loses absolute count scale when all evidence is duplicated; the proposed residual alone does not establish recurring intent. Histories also cannot establish purchase satisfaction, functional compatibility, or why preferences changed.",
  "implementation_notes": "Use only training histories and learned item embeddings. Review text, ratings, item categories, prices, stores, and simulator traits are unavailable; never fabricate them. Titles, descriptions, and timestamps are permitted but unnecessary for this initial experiment. Preserve all four category routes, baseline splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and trial-local artifacts. Keep execution single-GPU and account for every training, diagnostic, failed trial, and checkpoint evaluation within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget.\n\nInherit baseline architecture settings, optimizer, batch construction, sequence length, and loss unchanged for the representation comparison; serialize their resolved values. Honor SASREC_EPOCHS, whose host default is 200. Use recent window 5, cosine temperature 0.2, a bias-free Linear(2D,D) residual projection, and a scalar gate_logit initialized to -4. Initialize projection weights normally using the baseline initialization convention. Keep the embedding padding row zero and explicitly mask embeddings, pooled contexts, and final outputs at padded queries. Compute recent means with prefix cumulative sums and counts over positions t−4 through t. Use epsilon-safe normalization, causal key masks, and finite handling of empty rows before softmax. Vectorized historical pooling costs O(BL²D), with O(BL²) attention storage; vectorization does not make it linear.\n\nSave the complete module, configuration, and category routing, and update the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs the identical architecture. Its full-catalog unseen-item scoring must use the same fused representation and scoring function. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. view.model must reference the complete trained model; item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data retain their interfaces. Existing margin and embedding probes remain applicable. Category breakdowns must explicitly report unavailable metadata rather than invent categories. A B×L sampled-negative probe measures that diagnostic sampler, not the entire multi-negative training objective or validation HR@10.\n\nPrespecify baseline, residual-only, and loss-only comparisons before inspecting their validation results. Use the baseline checkpoint evaluation schedule unchanged and record it; choose the highest pinned macro validation HR@10, breaking checkpoint ties toward the earlier epoch and model ties toward unchanged SASRec. Do not tune per-category architectures independently in this initial comparison. Bound the planned runs using recorded baseline GPU costs, and log all configurations, checkpoint evaluations, failures, and GPU seconds. If budget permits mechanistic controls, prioritize an equally parameterized recent-only residual, then disjoint older-history pooling, then occurrence versus deduplicated pooling. Use a bias-free shared projection and the same gate settings; report residual RMS and include a scale-matched sensitivity analysis. Deduplicating IDs tests item multiplicity, not recurrence among distinct but related items. A frequency-weighted mean preserves relative counts, while a sum or explicit count feature changes absolute evidence scale and requires a separate, capacity- and scale-controlled proposal. Do not silently add such a mechanism to the selected model.\n\nFor the separate loss trial, retain unchanged SASRec and use 128 catalogue-uniform negatives per positive, sampled with replacement from nonpadding items. Mask draws matching that position’s target; retain other duplicates and history collisions, documenting this exact policy. Compute uncorrected sampled-softmax cross-entropy over the positive and remaining sampled logits. This is a sampled classification objective, not an unbiased full-softmax estimator; do not add an unjustified negative-only logQ correction. A gBCE alternative would require its own trial: the supplied official recommendation is K=256 and t=0.75, alpha=K/(catalogue_size−1), beta=1−t+alpha*t. Its official sampler permits collisions, so rejection would be an explicit deviation. These alternatives do not establish that harder negatives are needed.\n\nWhere pinned evaluator outputs permit, retain paired per-user hits for prespecified comparisons. Bootstrap 200 users with replacement independently within each category, preserving model pairing; use 10,000 CPU resamples with a fixed recorded seed, and report the macro difference, percentile 95% interval, category differences, and win/loss counts. One changed hit changes category HR by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR by 0.125 points. Optional exact McNemar tests assess discordant hits. Intervals describe user-sampling uncertainty conditional on candidates, training seeds, and searched models; they do not correct adaptive selection. Cached-prediction out-of-bag checkpoint analyses are exploratory, and extra training seeds measure training variability rather than independent confirmation. Freeze the full procedure before the host’s untouched final evaluation. Preserve the host evaluator throughout; sampled-candidate gains do not establish full-catalog usefulness. No execution or measured improvement is claimed.",
  "pseudocode": "# Baseline architecture, splits, routing, optimizer, and loss are inherited unchanged.\n# All tensor operations below are batched; sequence has shape B x L.\nclass InterestResidualSASRec:\n    def __init__(self, baseline, D):\n        self.sasrec = baseline\n        self.item_emb = baseline.item_emb\n        self.projection = Linear(2 * D, D, bias=False)\n        self.gate_logit = Parameter(-4.0)\n        # Initialize projection normally; do not zero both gate and branch.\n\n    def log2feats(self, sequence):\n        valid = sequence != 0\n        base = self.sasrec.log2feats(sequence)\n        emb = self.item_emb(sequence) * valid[..., None]\n        recent = causal_window_mean_from_prefix_sums(\n            emb, valid, window=5, denominator_clamp=1)\n        query = normalize(recent, eps=1e-8)\n        key = normalize(emb, eps=1e-8)\n        logits = batched_matmul(query, transpose(key)) / 0.2\n        allowed = causal_mask(L) & valid[:, None, :]\n        nonempty = allowed.any(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        logits = logits.masked_fill(~allowed, -inf)\n        logits = where(nonempty, logits, zeros_like(logits))\n        weights = softmax(logits, dim=-1)\n        weights = weights.masked_fill(~allowed, 0)\n        weights = weights / weights.sum(-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-8)\n        supported = batched_matmul(weights, emb)\n        residual = self.projection(concat(recent, supported, dim=-1))\n        fused = base + sigmoid(self.gate_logit) * residual\n        return fused * valid[..., None]\n\n    def predict_score(self, features, items):\n        return dot(features, self.item_emb(items))\n\n# Primary trials, using the same resolved baseline settings and pinned evaluator:\n# A: unchanged SASRec, unchanged loss.\n# B: residual SASRec, unchanged loss.\n# C: unchanged SASRec, 128-negative sampled-softmax objective.\n# Do not combine B and C before independent comparisons.\n# If budget permits, compare B against matched recent-only and older-only controls.\n# Older-only pooling excludes every position in the recent window; empty support = 0.\n# Remove/duplicate older support with the recent context fixed for mechanism probes.\n# Select by pinned macro HR@10; preserve all four category routes.\n# Serialize configuration and complete parameters; emit the matching predictor.",
