Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses item embeddings and positive-versus-negative 
scoring. Model internals are absent, so the sequence encoder’s architecture 
cannot be established. `log2feats(sequence)` provides position-level sequence 
representations; `predict_score(features, items)` converts those features and 
candidate IDs into logits. The probe evaluates valid sequence positions rather 
than explicitly extracting a final user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` receives the model-compatible view and stores 
its `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently 
used; review data and histories are not directly inspected.

The probe reads `item_emb.weight`, excluding padding row zero. For up to ten 
training batches `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, it switches to 
evaluation mode, computes features, stacks positive and negative IDs into shape 
`B × L × 2`, and scores them without gradients. Positions with positive ID zero 
are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings with seed 
42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the 
result using `(mean_cosine + 1) / 2`. Higher values indicate directional 
similarity; approximately 0.5 corresponds to zero mean cosine, not necessarily 
collapse.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive logit minus negative logit. Larger values suggest 
stronger sampled-pair separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction of negative margins; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction of margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts category occurrences 
separately for positive and negative items in weak-margin and incorrectly ranked
pairs, retaining the top 20 categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, or sensitivity testing occurs. Random
embedding subsampling estimates geometry; loader-provided negatives test 
pairwise discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
An optional interpreter prompt requests JSON containing `status`, 
`core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does not itself execute 
interpretation.

Diagnostics cover sampled training pairs, not validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, or generalization. Margins depend on score scale and negative sampling.
Mean cosine can conceal localized collapse. Item categories are unavailable 
under this task’s data contract, so category lists remain empty; counts must not
be fabricated. No ratings, review text, or simulator traits are measured.

