# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses item embedding geometry and positive–negative score 
separation. Model architecture is not shown. It accesses `item_emb.weight`, 
computes per-position sequence features through `log2feats(sequence)`, and 
scores candidate items with `predict_score(features, items)`. It does not 
explicitly extract or inspect a final user representation; how sequence features
are constructed depends on the model implementation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` expects the model or compatibility view to 
expose `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, `meta_data`, `review_data`, and
`user_train`. Reviews and histories are stored but unused by these probes.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped 
`B × L`. Up to ten batches are evaluated without gradients, with the model in 
evaluation mode. Positive and negative candidates are stacked into `B × L × 2`; 
positions with positive item ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples up to 2,048 non-padding item 
embeddings using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine 
similarities, and maps the result through `(mean_cosine + 1) / 2`. Higher values
indicate directional alignment and possible collapse; approximately orthogonal 
embeddings score around 0.5.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive minus negative logits. Larger values indicate stronger 
separation, including among difficult positions.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction below 0.5; lower indicates fewer 
weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts low-margin and wrong-ranking 
positions and lists the twenty most frequent metadata categories separately for 
positive and negative items. These are raw counts, not exposure-normalized 
failure rates.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, masking, substitution, or sensitivity tests occur. Random
embedding subsampling and loader-provided negative candidates are the only 
sampling mechanisms.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate 
interpreter prompt requests a JSON assessment containing `status`, 
`core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; this interpretation is not 
generated by the probe itself.

The probes measure training-pair separation, not validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, or recommendation diversity. Margins depend on logit scale and negative
sampling. Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists 
remain empty. No review information or simulator traits are measured. Empty 
margin samples return zeros, which can misleadingly resemble healthy error 
rates.

