Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The supplied code contains only the diagnosis module; the model architecture is 
not shown. Diagnosis uses `item_emb.weight` and per-position sequence features 
returned by `log2feats(sequence)`. It does not explicitly extract a final user 
representation or select the last sequence position. `predict_score(features, 
items)` supplies positive and negative logits.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the model or compatibility view and reads
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently 
accessed; reviews and stored histories are unused.

Training batches provide `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with shape B × 
L. The margin probe calls `eval()`, converts sequences to NumPy, computes 
features, and scores stacked positive/negative IDs. Positions with positive ID 
zero are excluded. Both probes disable gradients; the previous training mode is 
not restored.

# Probes & Metrics
- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal pairwise cosine 
similarities, and maps the result through `(cosine + 1) / 2`. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 means average cosine similarity 
near zero, not necessarily unhealthy embeddings.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive-minus-negative logits across valid positions from at most
ten batches. Higher values indicate stronger sampled training separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction with negative margin; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction with margin below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts categories of positive and 
negative items in low-margin and wrong-rank cases, retaining the top 20 
categories per group.

# Perturbation & Tests
No sequence shuffling, masking, replacement, or other sensitivity tests occur. 
Random embedding subsampling and supplied training negatives are the only 
sampling involved.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`; the category 
breakdown also includes thresholds and affected-position totals. A separate 
prompt requests an interpreted JSON summary with status, findings, implications,
and evidence.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal 
sensitivity, or simulator traits. Margins depend on logit scale and negative 
sampling. Categories are unavailable in this task, so category lists remain 
empty. Empty margin samples produce zeros that must not be interpreted as 
healthy results.

