{
  "description": "Strengthen the diagnostic adapter with bounded, conditionally matched history perturbations, and test whether its predefined recommendations provide useful guidance relative to a budget-matched gated recent-history baseline.",
  "motivation": "Existing probes measure embedding geometry and sampled training-pair separation. History interventions can investigate the qualitative complaint about broad relatedness, but recency, recurrence, popularity, positional changes, and unfamiliar inputs can confound interpretation. Diagnostic sensitivity and diagnostic cost-effectiveness therefore require separate evaluation; neither establishes user intent or guarantees HR@10 improvement.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device) and run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. Use view.model as the trained module and restore its original training mode in finally. Preserve existing embedding and margin probes; label their score-scale and sampled-negative limitations. Leave unavailable category breakdowns empty with an explicit unavailable reason. Do not use ratings, reviews, categories, prices, stores, inferred ownership, or simulator traits.\n\nFreeze the protocol before observing perturbation results. Per dataset, select up to 32 eligible training users using seed 42, and use their complete observed training histories truncated to the model's existing maximum length. Exclude held-out validation/test events and do not reconstruct prefixes from right-shifted loader targets. Require at least eight nonpadding interactions. Define recent positions as the last ceil(0.25*n) interactions. Define recurrent interest through repeated IDs or title/description TF-IDF cosine similarity >=0.5 to another observed prefix item, using a vocabulary fitted only on metadata for training-observed items. Freeze tokenization, vocabulary, threshold, and preprocessing; missing text supplies no lexical match. Record ID-based and lexical coverage separately. Similarity is an operational grouping rule, not established shared intent.\n\nPartition positions into recent-only, recurrent-only, overlapping, and neither. For each eligible group choose k=min(2, group size), retaining at least two interactions. For recurrence contrasts, sample five equal-count controls without replacement within each draw from nonrecurrent positions matched on relative-position quartile, elapsed-time bin, training-frequency quartile, and final-item status. Use elapsed-time bins <=7 days, >7 to 30 days, >30 to 180 days, and >180 days relative to the prefix endpoint; missing timestamps form a separate stratum. Count item frequency from training interactions only, and save bin edges. Require exact stratum-count matches; skip infeasible contrasts and report coverage rather than silently relaxing matching. Recent-only contrasts use equal-count nonrecent controls matched on popularity and recurrence status; position/time differences define that contrast and remain inseparable from it. Treat overlapping-group contrasts as joint sensitivity, not isolated recurrence effects. An isolated-interest contrast uses nonrecurrent positions outside the recent group with controls matched on position/time/popularity where feasible; report unavailable when the partition leaves no valid comparator. Fine strata may make these analyses sparse.\n\nFor the primary diagnostic, use one fixed full-catalog candidate set per user excluding all items in the original observed training history. Keep that set unchanged after interventions so removed items never become eligible. Do not add validation/test labels to eligibility decisions. Cache baseline scores and use chunked scoring with deterministic item-ID tie breaking. Report top-10 overlap as intersection size divided by 10, displacement as perturbed rank minus baseline rank of the original top item, and the original top-versus-runner-up score gap evaluated on those same two items. Score-gap changes remain scale dependent. Subtract the mean matched-control change from each targeted change; aggregate first within user, then within dataset. Bootstrap users within datasets for descriptive intervals, keeping all controls for a user together. These intervals do not quantify training-seed variation or prove causal preference.\n\nCompact deletion follows the baseline's left-padding convention. Fixed-slot masking is available only after checking the actual architecture's position IDs, attention key exclusions, zero-query behavior, and final readout. Never assume an internal zero excludes an attention key. If masking requires changing the trained architecture's attention semantics, report it unavailable rather than presenting it as an equivalent intervention. Final-position masking needs a separately defined readout and must be reported separately or omitted. Shuffle only nonpadding history and include a last-item-fixed permutation control. Check shapes, finite outputs, baseline identity, deterministic ties, position assignments, and mode restoration. Positive score rescaling should preserve rank diagnostics while changing margins. Under independent continuous random scores, expected pinned HR@10 is 0.10 for 100 candidates; finite realizations fluctuate.\n\nPredeclare a maximum diagnostic allocation of 5% of the remaining shared GPU-second budget, with measured runtime included. A predefined decision rule may nominate the gated residual only if the recurrence contrast has positive mean excess top-10 disruption in at least three datasets and adequate matched coverage, defined beforehand as at least 16 of the 32 sampled users per qualifying dataset. This is a heuristic nomination threshold, not a significance claim. Insufficient coverage produces an inconclusive diagnosis. The nominated change is tested once; it is never applied automatically. Run one equal-GPU-time direct gated-residual comparator regardless of probe outcome, reuse the same trained baseline, and log all costs and trials. This small comparison is exploratory evidence about utility, not a controlled general demonstration that diagnostics improve search.\n\nFor the comparator, mix the baseline final feature h with a projected mean of the last five nonpadding item embeddings: h_mix=(1-g)*h+g*W*pool, with scalar g=sigmoid(b), initialized to 0.1. Retain baseline item scoring, loss, optimizer, and training settings to isolate this change. Update the predictor writer and working/predict.py together if this model is trained. Select checkpoints and trials exclusively through the pinned four-dataset macro validation HR@10. If per-user outcomes are available from the pinned evaluator, use paired within-category user bootstraps for model differences without changing candidates or evaluator behavior. Such intervals do not correct adaptive validation reuse.\n\nPreserve all four dataset routes, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], single-GPU execution, trial-local artifacts, and SASREC_EPOCHS environment behavior with the task default of 200. Diagnostics alone require no predictor modification. Full-catalog diagnostics remain supplementary to pinned sampled HR@10. Twenty qualitative training users provide case evidence only. Keep the final held-out evaluation separate and unavailable during search.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    def __init__(self, view, device):\n        self.view, self.device = view, device\n\n    def run_full_diagnosis(self, train_loader):\n        was_training = self.view.model.training\n        try:\n            self.view.model.eval()\n            with no_grad():\n                retain_existing_embedding_and_margin_probes(train_loader)\n                for user, prefix in frozen_training_prefix_sample(seed=42, limit=32):\n                    candidates = catalog_minus_original_observed_history(user)\n                    baseline = score_in_chunks(prefix, candidates)\n                    groups = frozen_recent_recurrent_partition(prefix)\n                    for contrast in predefined_contrasts(groups):\n                        target, controls = exact_matched_subsets(\n                            contrast, max_removed=2, repeats=5, seed=42)\n                        if controls_are_infeasible(target, controls):\n                            record_unavailable_with_reason(contrast)\n                            continue\n                        for operation in verified_supported_operations():\n                            target_scores = score_in_chunks(operation(prefix, target), candidates)\n                            control_scores = [\n                                score_in_chunks(operation(prefix, subset), candidates)\n                                for subset in controls]\n                            record_rank_changes_and_control_adjusted_differences(\n                                baseline, target_scores, control_scores,\n                                tie_break='item_id')\n                    record_last_item_fixed_shuffle_control(prefix, candidates)\n                    stop_at_predeclared_probe_budget()\n                metrics = aggregate_by_user_dataset_and_history_length()\n                metrics.update(coverage_runtime_and_user_bootstrap_intervals())\n                definitions = metric_formulas_controls_missingness_and_limits()\n                return {'metrics': metrics, 'metric_definitions': definitions}\n        finally:\n            self.view.model.train(was_training)\n\n# Separate, predefined experiment orchestration:\n# 1. Run one budget-matched gated-residual comparator regardless of probe outcome.\n# 2. Allow at most one additional probe-nominated experiment under the frozen rule.\n# 3. Update predictor writer for any architecture change.\n# 4. Select only by pinned macro validation HR@10 and log all GPU costs.",
  "originality": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "Combines recurrence-sensitive controls, explicit matching coverage, SASRec-specific intervention checks, and a budget-matched direct comparator.",
    "negative": "Perturbations, conditional matching, and gated pooling are established ingredients; the contribution is a task-specific protocol whose validity remains empirical."
  },
