Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses a model through a SASRec-compatible view; model 
internals are not shown. It reads base item embeddings from 
`view.item_emb.weight`, excluding padding item 0. Sequence representations come 
from `view.log2feats(sequence)` and feed into `view.predict_score(features, 
items)`. The probe scores every valid sequence position; it does not explicitly 
select a final user representation. How representations are computed internally 
cannot be determined here.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the actual `view.model`, training 
histories, metadata and review-data references. Histories and metadata are 
unused by the active probes; no review content is inspected.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching `B × L`
tensors. Positions count only when sequence, positive and negative IDs are all 
nonzero. Shape mismatches and nonfinite sampled embeddings or scores raise 
errors.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Sample up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings using 
seed 42, normalize them, compute mean pairwise cosine, and map it to `[0,1]`. A 
score of 0.5 means zero mean cosine; higher values indicate directional 
alignment, without establishing collapse or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Across at most ten training batches, 
calculate positive score minus sampled-negative score. Larger mean and 
10th-percentile margins indicate stronger separation; smaller 
negative-beats-positive and margin-below-0.5 rates are preferable. Absolute 
margins depend on score scale.
- **Coverage and scale:** `margin_valid_positions` counts usable positions. 
`sampled_logit_std` measures score dispersion on the first usable batch, not 
accuracy.
- **Breakdown:** Count weak-margin and incorrect-ranking positions. Category 
lists remain empty because categories are unavailable.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, ablations or sensitivity tests. Diagnosis 
runs without gradients in evaluation mode, seeds diagnostic randomness to 1042, 
and restores managed random states and every module’s prior training mode 
afterward.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
Metrics contain embedding alignment, four margin summaries, nested breakdown 
counts, valid-position count and sampled-logit standard deviation. Unavailable 
numerical measurements are `null`.

These bounded training probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, behavioral traits, diversity, gradients or robustness. The separate 
interpreter prompt requests a JSON interpretation containing `status`, 
`core_findings`, `key_implications` and metric evidence; the probe itself 
returns raw measurements.

