Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The model implementation is not included; diagnosis accesses it through a 
SASRec-compatible view. Relevant hooks are `item_emb.weight`, 
`log2feats(sequence)` for per-position representations, and 
`predict_score(features, items)` for candidate logits. Final-position probes use
`log2feats(sequence)[:, -1:, :]` as the user representation. Optional backbone 
and recent-item pooling hooks expose branch contributions.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view, actual module 
(`view.model`), histories, and metadata. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` with B × L tensors. Diagnosis reads at most ten batches, 
excluding padding, zero candidate IDs, and identical positive/negative pairs. It
caches up to sixteen valid users from the first suitable batch for sensitivity 
tests.

The actual module runs in evaluation mode without gradients. Original submodule 
modes and global Python, NumPy, PyTorch, and CUDA RNG states are restored 
afterward; loader-owned state is not restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings, 
computes mean off-diagonal cosine similarity, and maps it to `[0,1]`. Higher 
values indicate stronger directional alignment; 0.5 means zero mean cosine. This
alone does not establish unhealthy collapse.
- **Positive/negative separation:** Computes positive minus sampled-negative 
logits at valid training positions. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins 
indicate stronger separation. Lower negative-wins and small-margin rates are 
preferable; “small” means margin below 0.5.
- **Recent dependence:** Reports fixed-candidate logit sensitivity, 
affected-user counts, and an unchanged-input numerical control. Optional hooks 
report recent-branch scale, representation norms, and branch-removal effects. 
Sensitivity magnitude has no universal good/bad threshold.

# Perturbation & Tests

For cached users, masks the final five sequence positions or the preceding five 
with zeros, then measures logit-change RMS only among users whose histories 
changed. Candidates remain fixed. Optional branch removal scores backbone-only 
representations. These test encoder dependence, not causal effects or ranking 
improvements.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`. Metrics include
`embedding_collapse_score`, four `pos_neg_*` separation statistics, 
`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`, and nested `recent_dependence` 
measurements.

Unavailable measurements use nulls or availability flags. Item-category 
breakdown is explicitly unavailable. Probes do not measure validation HR@10, 
full-catalog recommendation quality, diversity, simulator traits, or graph 
contributions outside `predict_score`. A separate interpreter prompt requests a 
grounded JSON assessment with status, findings, implications, and evidence.

