INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for diagnosis in iteration 3:
{
  "description": "Add a causal recent-five-position embedding mean to SASRec features through one zero-initialized learned scalar per dataset. Compare unchanged SASRec, a last-item residual, and a uniform mean over the visible causal prefix. Retain this as an early-stage empirical control study rather than claim a new fusion principle.",
  "motivation": "The diagnosis suggests that recent, repeated interests can provide more specific evidence than broad historical relevance. Pooling tests local interaction content, but does not explicitly identify repeated interests or infer ownership, compatibility, or current requirements. FPMC and especially FOSSIL establish close precedents; the useful contribution would be a reproducible, compute-accounted comparison on the four target categories.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four dataset routes, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, and existing SASREC_EPOCHS handling with effective environment default 200. Use existing tied item embeddings, the original feature computation, score function, negative sampling, loss, optimizer, and padding rules for the primary comparison. Register one scalar per separately trained dataset model after baseline initialization, without additional random draws. Place the residual after the backbone's final feature transformation and before unchanged scoring; do not introduce a subsequent normalization. At alpha=0, predictions match the backbone for identical inputs in evaluation mode, but subsequent training trajectories need not match. Shared embeddings continue receiving baseline gradients; parameters exclusive to a zero-gated branch would initially receive zero task gradients. Define recent-five as the five causal sequence slots ending at t, excluding zero IDs from numerator and denominator. On ordinarily contiguous right-aligned histories this equals the latest five available items; interior diagnostic masks retain their original positions. Compute sums and counts with a zero-prefixed cumulative sum, clamp denominators to at least one, and return zero for empty windows. The uniform control averages the visible causal prefix within the model's truncated input, not an unavailable full history. Save residual mode, window, gate, and architecture configuration in checkpoints and reproduce them in the predictor writer. Expose augmented features through log2feats, keep predict_score unchanged, retain view.item_emb and view.model as the actual trained module, and provide backbone/pool hooks for branch ablation. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions for B x L sequence/positive/negative batches. Preserve numerical controls, RNG restoration, mode restoration, and unavailable-data flags. Do not assume the adapter's illustrative ratings or review fields exist. Use only public training interactions, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Record gate trajectories, feature/branch norms, and training-popularity versus embedding-norm association; these diagnostics do not establish improvement. Use the four primary variants before optional fixed-gate, small-nonzero-gate, normalized-scoring, frozen-backbone, or FOSSIL-style lag-weight experiments. Prioritize train-only popularity bias and a learned global logit-temperature control if compute permits: positive global temperature cannot change fixed-checkpoint within-user ranking, but can change training gradients. A learned scalar may become negative; report its sign rather than assume positive recent-interest amplification. Treat last-item-preserving order shuffles as backbone-order probes because a mean is invariant to permutations within its window. Older-window and popularity/length-matched cross-user replacements require explicit matching and remain distribution-shift probes. Prespecify primary window=5, validation cadence, checkpoint rule, exact tie-breaking, and per-variant cumulative GPU-second caps in the executable trial configuration before observing new results. Retain baseline cadence and checkpoint behavior for matched comparisons; if they are unavailable, their exact values remain a required implementation specification. Count tuning, diagnostics, debugging, failed trials, and checkpoint evaluations against 43,200 GPU-seconds. Report actual compute, update counts, training exposure, validation looks, and best validation performance versus consumed compute; equal epochs alone do not establish equal budgets. Use training seed 42 for required comparisons. Select exclusively on the host's pinned 200-users/category, 99-unique-negative, seed-42 validation macro HR@10. Report four category HRs and their equally weighted mean, plus training-history-length and target training-popularity strata. For descriptive uncertainty, perform 10,000 paired bootstrap replicates using a separate local RNG seeded 42: independently resample 200 users with replacement within each category, preserve each user's paired outcomes across models, equally average the four hit-rate differences, and report the 2.5th/97.5th percentiles. This conditions on fixed datasets, candidates, and checkpoints and excludes training/candidate randomness and adaptive-selection correction. Optional full-catalog validation diagnostics must exclude seen items, retain the validation target, and must not replace pinned selection; report rank correlation and pairwise model-winner agreement with sampled evaluation. The twenty training-user simulator cases remain exploratory: report individual outcomes and denominators without population satisfaction or latent-trait claims. Freeze all selections before independent held-out evaluation; never inspect hidden test files or revise from test results.",
  "pseudocode": "Before new results:\n    Freeze four primary variants, window=5, validation cadence,\n    checkpoint rule, tie-breaking, and cumulative compute caps\n    Preserve preprocessing seed 0 and training seed 42\nFor each variant and each of the four dataset routes:\n    Initialize baseline SASRec exactly as before\n    Register alpha = 0 without consuming random draws\n    For each batch while the declared training/compute limit permits:\n        h = backbone.log2feats(sequence)\n        mask = (sequence != 0)\n        e = item_emb(sequence) * mask[..., None]\n        if variant == baseline:\n            z = h\n        else:\n            if variant == last_item:\n                pool = e\n            if variant == recent_mean:\n                pool = window_sum(e, 5) / clamp(window_sum(mask, 5), min=1)\n            if variant == uniform_prefix:\n                pool = cumsum(e) / clamp(cumsum(mask), min=1)\n            z = h + alpha * pool\n        Apply unchanged candidate scoring and valid-position training loss\n        Update using the matched optimizer and sampling configuration\n        At prespecified looks, obtain pinned validation outcomes\n        Save checkpoints using the frozen rule; log compute and exposure\n    Save architecture configuration and trained state beneath trial directory\nGenerate working/predict.py with identical routing, feature, and score computations\nRun DiagnosisProbe through the augmented SASRec-compatible view\nSelect by pinned macro validation HR@10 using frozen tie-breaking\nReport category HRs, paired differences, descriptive bootstrap intervals, and total cost\nFreeze the selected predictor before the host's independent held-out evaluation",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "A zero-start residual with matched SASRec controls provides a precise empirical test of the diagnosed local-interest hypothesis.",
    "negative": "FPMC, FOSSIL, adaptive long/short-term fusion, and ReZero already establish the main ingredients; neither recent means nor scalar fusion is new."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "A reproducible gain beyond popularity and optimization controls could motivate later research on when local evidence helps contextual sequence models.",
    "negative": "The intervention may only improve this sampled-ranking objective and cannot establish practical compatibility, current intent, or a broadly useful new architecture."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "The core branch uses linear-time cumulative sums and one scalar per dataset without adding a separate neural encoder.",
    "negative": "Reproducible checkpoint selection, cumulative compute accounting, padding semantics, and consistency across prediction and diagnosis require more work than the branch itself."
  }
}


