# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe accesses the trained `nn.Module` through a compatibility adapter; 
model architecture is not shown. `view.log2feats(sequence)` produces B × L × D 
features. The final user representation is `features[:, -1, :]`, computed from 
the latest L interactions, left-padded with zeros. `view.predict_score` converts
features and item IDs into logits; `view.item_emb` supplies catalog embeddings.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` snapshots 
`view.user_train` histories and optional timestamps. It never consumes 
`train_loader`; training-margin batches are generated independently. Optional 
dataset routing and five supplied user IDs identify the exploratory panel. 
Missing panels are reported without sampling replacements.

Diagnosis runs in evaluation and inference modes, restoring module flags and 
Python, NumPy, and torch RNG states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **History sensitivity:** Measures top-10 overlap, displacement of original 
top-10 items in full-catalog ranks, strict pair-order reversals, mean absolute 
logit change, and final-feature L2 change. Higher overlap and smaller changes 
indicate stability, not accuracy.
- **Training margins:** Samples 320 eligible-user draws with replacement and 
teacher-forced transitions, using uniform negatives outside each user’s complete
training history. Reports mean margin, empirical p10, negative-beats-positive 
rate, and margin-below-0.5 rate. Larger margins suggest better sampled training 
separation, subject to logit scale.
- **Embedding geometry:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings. Reports 
mean cosine, normalized effective rank from centered singular values, leading 
singular-value mass, norms, and zero counts. Strong alignment or concentrated 
spectra can flag restricted geometry but do not establish collapse.

# Perturbation & Tests

Edits include identity, recent/old deletion, last-item-only, anchor-preserving 
deletion, random deletion, full shuffle, and prefix shuffle. Stochastic edits 
use five seeded draws. Each user retains the same full-catalog candidate pool 
excluding their complete original history.

Matched contrasts compare deletion location and final-item preservation. Edits 
compact positions, so content and positional effects are intertwined. Identity, 
repeated-inference, and positive-rescaling checks audit consistency.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include
panel metadata, baseline audits, edit aggregates, paired contrasts, per-draw 
records, margins, geometry, failures/counts, provenance hashes, integrity 
checks, and diagnostic cost. Full rank arrays remain in `rank_cache`.

Aggregates weight users equally and include exploratory bootstrap intervals. 
Five-user panels are not representative. No validation accuracy, semantic 
sensitivity, simulator traits, or causal improvement is established. 
Four-category aggregation is external; host macro validation HR@10 remains the 
sole selection metric.

